 "result": "Fixed the root cause: `teams.key` is uniquely constrained per organization, so the earlier design (three teams all keyed `ENG`) violated a DB constraint on install.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Gave each team a distinct key: target `ENG`, name-decoy `PLAT` (doesn't contain \"ENG\"), description-decoy `ENGOPS`, private-decoy `ENGQA` — all unique, satisfying the constraint.\n- Changed the key filter's operator from `eq` to `contains_ci` on `\"ENG\"`, so the description/private decoys (whose keys start with ENG but aren't literally \"ENG\") still satisfy that condition, while the name-decoy (`PLAT`) correctly fails it.\n- Updated the request text to \"the private team keyed ENG\" and refreshed decoy explanations to reference the new key values.\n\nThe decoy logic itself is unchanged: name-vs-key confusion (F1), name-vs-description confusion (F1), and the flipped `private` flag (F0).",
